# Purpose
# Run browser based visual, DOM, keyboard, console, network, and target size checks.
#
# Common usage
# Run from the repository root with localhost already serving _site.
# .\scripts\verify-browser-pages.ps1
# .\scripts\verify-browser-pages.ps1 -BaseUri http://127.0.0.1:4000
# .\scripts\verify-browser-pages.ps1 -Browser Chrome
# .\scripts\verify-browser-pages.ps1 -OutputDirectory verification-artifacts\manual-check
# .\scripts\verify-browser-pages.ps1 -DisplayViewports "3440x1440@1","1920x1080@2"
# .\scripts\verify-browser-pages.ps1 -DisplayViewports "3440x1440@1" -SkipScreenshots -SkipVisualValidation
# .\scripts\verify-browser-pages.ps1 -UpdateVisualBaselines
#
# Useful options
# -BaseUri chooses the local site URL.
# -Browser chooses Auto, Chrome, Edge, or Chromium.
# -OutputDirectory chooses where reports and screenshots are written.
# -DisplayViewports chooses wide and high-DPI cases using WIDTHxHEIGHT@DPR syntax.
# -SkipScreenshots skips screenshot capture.
# -SkipVisualValidation skips visual artifact validation.
# -VisualBaselineDirectory chooses a baseline folder.
# -UpdateVisualBaselines refreshes visual baselines.
# -RequireVisualBaselines fails when a baseline is missing.
# -KeepBrowser leaves the browser open for debugging.
#
# Recommended next command
# .\scripts\verify-visual-artifacts.ps1 -ArtifactDirectory verification-artifacts\manual-check
#
# Notes
# Prefer verify-pages.ps1 for full local verification.
# This script expects a running local server.
# Default display profiles include 3440x1440@1 for 34-inch ultrawide WQHD and high-DPI DPR cases.
